  + A plain log file gets **no** structure block and no aggregate block, so an old-style invocation is byte-identical to before (verified by running both). Day 177 (@yuanhao on #810) added **`EXCLUDED_NO_HARNESS_OUTPUT`**, because **an absent input was scoring as a measured zero**. Reproduced verbatim at HEAD before the fix: `printf '' > empty.log; python3 scripts/measure_abstentions.py empty.log` → `empty.log abstentions=0 firings=0 fallback=0 gradeable=no prose_excluded=0`, i.e. a 0-byte file printed the *same row a genuinely healthy session prints*. How it bit: a shell-quoting slip made three `gh run view --log` redirect targets wrong, each log came back 0 bytes, and the instrument reported three clean sessions and `NOT YET GRADEABLE: 0 of 4` — exactly the shape of a healthy stretch. Re-fetched, those logs were 114KB/194KB/253KB and genuinely 0-abstention, so the error would have produced **a true conclusion by luck**, the worst kind to catch late. This is my own rule landing on my own tool — *"could not check" must never read as "checked; clean"*, the refusal the pre-push hook makes, the refusal `CiScan`'s could-not-run branch makes, the refusal `UngradedScan`'s unread-lines clause makes — one level up from the anchoring rule: never let an **absent** input stand in for a measured zero. It failed in the flattering direction, every unreadable log silently shrinking the denominator toward a healthier answer, inside the one instrument whose whole job is deciding whether the #808 gate works. **The anchor is a harness marker, not byte size**, and that choice is the point: byte size misses the subtler case — a truncated or partially-downloaded log which *has* bytes and no phase line, and which scored clean too. The decision half is the pure, table-tested pair `classify_harness_output_line(line)` (the marker name or `None`) and `classify_harness_output(line)` (marker + prose flag), with `has_harness_output(lines)` as the presence fold and all I/O at the call site. Six markers, each an `echo` to stdout in `scripts/evolve.sh` (`:136` `=== Day N (DATE HH:MM) ===`, `:1167` `Phase A1: Assessment (Ns)...`, `:1291` `Phase A2: Planning (Ns)...`, `:1709` `Phase B: Implementation...`, `:1784` `→ Task N: <title> [<kind>]`, `:3586` `=== Day N complete ===`), each matched from its first word to end-of-line with only counters/timeouts/titles loose and the `gh run view` runner prefix (`job\tjob\tTIMESTAMP`) allowed in front — the same anchoring `classify_line` uses, and **any one** of the six is enough. The `=== SECTION ===` banners near `evolve.sh:1175`/`:1313` are deliberately **not** markers: they live inside heredocs composing *prompt text*, so anchoring on them would accept a log containing nothing but an echoed prompt. Every candidate still runs through `is_quoted_prose`, which is load-bearing rather than ceremony here — #810's own thread, the commissioning task file and this very paragraph all contain the literal strings `Phase A1` and `Phase A2`, so without it a log holding only my own prose *about* the detector would be judged a real session, the permissive direction that reinstates the bug; a shape-match that trips the filter is **counted** (`harness_markers_quoted=N` on the row), never silently dropped. The bucket is excluded from numerator **and** denominator, **counted and reported** in the verdict, and **never** summed into `INELIGIBLE`, `UNKNOWN_AGE`, `EXCLUDED_PROVIDER_ERROR` or the zero-abstention exclusions (the provider-error list is filtered to stay disjoint so nothing is counted twice). A third state is kept distinct in the code and not just in prose: `harness_markers is None` — no line stream was folded at all, reachable only from a hand-built fixture — is **not** this bucket, because *nobody looked* is not *nothing was there*. `MIN_GRADEABLE_SESSIONS = 4` is **unchanged**, and `NOT YET GRADEABLE` becoming more common is the correct outcome rather than a regression. **The positive control was run, because the mirror failure is worse than the bug**: a wrong marker set makes *every* real session excluded, the denominator goes to zero, and the tool reports `NOT YET GRADEABLE` forever — the same "cannot fail loudly" defect wearing the opposite sign, and quieter. Control: run **`32777115768`** (`gh run view … --log`, 239,103 bytes) scores **not excluded**, and all six markers fire on it individually (`SESSION_HEADER` 1, `PHASE_A1` 1, `PHASE_A2` 1, `PHASE_B` 1, `TASK_START` 2, `SESSION_FOOTER` 1, `prose_excluded` 0) — so the set is exercised by a real log and not only by fixtures. A log that carries markers is **byte-identical** to the pre-bucket tool (verified by running both), which is the whole common path and was the regression risk; `classify_line`, `classify`, `classify_provider_error`, `is_quoted_prose` and the anchored matching were **not** touched. **What it cannot do, stated rather than implied:** it detects an *absent or marker-less* input, never a log that is **complete but wrong** — a full session log whose contents are misleading passes exactly as an honest one does; and it cannot tell a genuinely quiet session from one whose markers **changed wording in a future `evolve.sh`**, which is a protected file I may not edit and therefore cannot pin with a drift test the way `GLOBAL_SETTERS` is pinned by `every_named_setter_still_exists` — if those six echoes are reworded, every session silently becomes `EXCLUDED_NO_HARNESS_OUTPUT` and the only symptom is a permanent `NOT YET GRADEABLE`. **Ordinal collision, recorded rather than quietly renumbered:** the paragraph above calls `EXCLUDED_PROVIDER_ERROR` "the fourth exclusion bucket" and #810's task file calls this one "a fourth exclusion bucket" too — both were counting from a different starting point, so the buckets are referred to **by name, never by ordinal**, and neither sentence is edited to invent an agreement that did not exist.
