What I changed: one commit, CLAUDE.md only. The scripts/measure_abstentions.py paragraph now names EXCLUDED_NO_HARNESS_OUTPUT, records the 0-byte reproduction verbatim, explains why the anchor is a harness marker rather than byte size (a truncated log has bytes and no phase line, and scored clean too), lists the six evolve.sh echoes, and says why the heredoc === SECTION === banners are deliberately excluded.

What I verified rather than inherited:

• All six line numbers re-checked against `sed -n '136p;1167p;1291p;1709p;1784p;3586p' scripts/evolve.sh` — they match the real echo shapes.
• Positive control re-run: `gh run view 32777115768 --log (239,103 bytes) scores **not excluded**, and all six markers fire on it individually (SESSION_HEADER 1, PHASE_A1 1, PHASE_A2 1, PHASE_B 1, TASK_START 2, SESSION_FOOTER 1, prose_excluded` 0). That matters because the mirror failure is quieter than the bug: a wrong marker set excludes every real session and reports NOT YET GRADEABLE forever.
• Byte-identity actually diffed rather than asserted: HEAD~1's script vs. current on that same log → identical output.
• --test exits 0; cargo fmt, clippy -D warnings, build, test (5099 passed, 0 failed) all green.

Two things I recorded rather than smoothed over:

• The limits, stated plainly in the doc: it detects an absent or marker-less input, never a log that is complete but wrong; and it cannot notice a future evolve.sh rewording of those six echoes. evolve.sh is protected, so unlike GLOBAL_SETTERS I cannot pin the marker set with a drift test — if the wording changes, every session silently becomes excluded and the only symptom is a permanent NOT YET GRADEABLE.
• An ordinal collision: the existing paragraph calls EXCLUDED_PROVIDER_ERROR "the fourth exclusion bucket" and #810's task file calls this one "a fourth exclusion bucket" too. Both counted from different starting points. I referred to the buckets by name and left both sentences intact rather than renumbering one to invent an agreement that never existed.

